  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "When a string is divided into three segments of length $l_{1}, l_{2},$ and $l_{3}$, the fundamental frequencies of these three segments are $v_{1}, v_{2}$ and $v_{3}$ respectively. The original fundamental frequency\r\n\r\n(v) of the string is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Vn0ma",
      "text": "$\\quad \\sqrt{v}=\\sqrt{v_{1}}+\\sqrt{v_{2}}+\\sqrt{v_{3}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cfXsI",
      "text": "$v=v_{1}+v_{2}+v_{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Qu9v8",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{v}=\\frac{1}{v_{1}}+\\frac{1}{v_{2}}+\\frac{1}{v_{3}}$.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "70ysT",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{v}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{v_{1}}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{v_{2}}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{v_{3}}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Fundamental frequency is given by\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nv=\\frac{1}{2 l} \\sqrt{\\frac{T}{\\mu}} \\Rightarrow v \\propto \\frac{1}{l} \\Rightarrow P \\propto \\frac{1}{v}\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nSince, $P$ divided into $l_{1}, l_{2}$ and $l_{3}$ segments Here $l=l_{1}+l_{2}+l_{3}$\r\n\r\nSo $\\quad \\frac{1}{v}=\\frac{1}{v_{1}}+\\frac{1}{v_{2}}+\\frac{1}{v_{3}}$",
    "image": null
